  "scope": "The previous final-step eligibility guard is retained, with additional explicitly reviewed item callbacks. Type boosts and critical-rate changes are evaluated before damage variance and have no dependence on post-hit HP. Status cures and PP restoration depend only on alive/dead status or non-HP state; banned damaging statuses and confusion cannot be introduced by the approved moves. Mail item-taking callbacks are unreachable with these moves. Berserk Gene remains excluded. All rejected cells use the previous exact path. Projected final-step kernels are audited against exact native outcome probabilities; other cells are checked against native raw-state kernels. Every ledger, policy, controller query, mixture and ceiling is independently checked. Two runs per backend and zero/500ms controls are included. The 1440-case HP/item/move grid includes active Rock, Ice and Steel boost items. A further 48 cases cover Farfetchd with Stick, Chansey with Lucky Punch and Mystery Berry PP restoration; the tests require the critical items to change actual outcome probabilities and PP restoration to occur in both enumerators. Existing unsafe-effect and sandstorm fallback controls are retained. This is a source-reviewed argument plus finite testing, not a machine-checked proof over all engine states. Time excludes input loading, model replay and independent audits. No production integration or deployed-strength claim."
